{% extends 'base.html.jinja' %}
{% from 'evidence.html.jinja' import human_evidence, page_evidence %}
{% from 'charts.html.jinja' import performance_header, detection_overview, page_comparison %}

{% block document_title %}{{ title }}: {{ model_name }}; {{ manifest.run_id }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<section id="performance" aria-labelledby="performance-title">
{{ performance_header(cost, token_usage, model_prices) }}
{{ detection_overview(rates) }}
{{ page_comparison(pages) }}
</section>
<section id="human-findings" aria-labelledby="findings-title">
<h2 id="findings-title">Human findings</h2>
<p>Each original Human finding appears once in source order. Open View details to read the original Human finding, then View Page Decisions to read the review decision and matched tool findings. Global findings include a separate page decisions dropdown for every page. Details and page decisions start collapsed.</p>
{% include 'controls.html.jinja' %}
<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Human findings table" tabindex="0">
<table id="findings">
<caption>Original Human findings and combined detection outcomes</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Issue title</th><th scope="col">WCAG</th><th scope="col">Scope</th><th scope="col">Expected source</th><th scope="col">LLM</th><th scope="col">Programmatic checks</th><th scope="col">Details</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for row in rows %}
<tr data-expected="{{ row.expected }}" data-llm="{{ row.llm_outcome }}" data-programmatic="{{ row.programmatic_outcome }}">
<th scope="row">{{ row.human.problem }}</th><td data-print-label="WCAG">{{ row.human.raw_evidence['WCAG Sc'] }}</td><td data-print-label="Scope">{% if row.human.page_scope == 'global' %}Global{% else %}Page-local{% endif %}</td><td data-print-label="Expected source">{{ row.expected }}</td><td data-print-label="LLM">{{ row.llm_outcome }}</td><td data-print-label="Programmatic checks">{{ row.programmatic_outcome }}</td>
<td><p data-selected-page-result hidden></p><div data-search-matches></div><details><summary>View details</summary><div class="evidence">
<div data-evidence-location="Original Human finding">{{ human_evidence(row) }}</div>
{% if row.human.page_scope == 'global' %}
<h3>Combined result</h3>
<p>Expected source: {{ row.expected }}. Combined LLM: {{ row.llm_outcome }}. Combined Programmatic checks: {{ row.programmatic_outcome }}. Any complete catch on one page earns combined credit once for that source; partial evidence across pages earns none.</p>
<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Page decisions for {{ row.human.problem }}" tabindex="0">
<table><caption>Every page decision for {{ row.human.problem }}</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Page</th><th scope="col">Expected source</th><th scope="col">LLM</th><th scope="col">Programmatic checks</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for page in row.pages %}<tr data-page-table-row="{{ page.source_url }}"><th scope="row">{{ page.source_url }}</th><td>{{ page.expected }}</td><td>{{ page.llm_outcome }}</td><td>{{ page.programmatic_outcome }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% endif %}
{% for page in row.pages %}{{ page_evidence(page) }}{% endfor %}
</div></details></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
</section>
{% include 'method.html.jinja' %}
<section id="combined-method" aria-labelledby="combined-method-title"><h2 id="combined-method-title">Full evaluation scoring</h2>
<p>Eligibility is established independently of detection. If any page is testable for a Global finding, the finding enters that expected source's denominator once. All testable pages must agree on the source. Findings not testable on any page remain in Overall and outside the LLM and Programmatic denominators.</p>
<p>Pages can have different numbers of local and testable findings. Repeated Global findings contribute to each page's results but only once to combined results. Combined rates use original finding counts; page rates must not be added or averaged.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
